From a0acf0949a992a42f3588b50db40c4f0d4181dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:27:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Block on worker results instead of polling finished
 threads

The coordinator counted busy workers with JoinHandle::is_finished, but a
worker sends its result before its thread finishes. After receiving a
result the wait loop still saw that worker running and waited out a
20 ms recv_timeout, so with one thread every picture took 20 ms longer.
It now counts pictures dispatched but not yet reported, raised at
dispatch and lowered for each result received, and waits with a
blocking recv, which returns because a dispatched worker always sends,
even after a panic. The handles stay for joining in flush and Drop.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Sonnet 5.5)
